From 9ce4bdc99a9431dc0141a472be30c929d6bf9187 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (audit & migration)" <claude@users.noreply.anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:43:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] security(uploads): fix remote code execution via warranty
 attachment upload

Warranty attachments were saved under public/uploads with the client-supplied extension and no
content validation, so an authenticated user could upload a .php file and run it.

- Validate by file content (finfo) against an allowlist (JPG/PNG/WEBP/GIF/PDF); the stored extension
  is derived from the sniffed type, never from the client name. Max 10 MB.
- Store attachments outside the web root (UPLOADS_DIR, default storage/uploads) with 0640 files.
- Serve files via short-lived HMAC-signed links bound to attachment id, tenant and expiry
  (GET /api/v1/warranty/attachments/{id}/file) with nosniff + CSP sandbox headers.
- Verify the warranty request belongs to the caller's tenant before attaching.
- Resolve legacy files only for allowlisted extensions and plain file names.
- Drop SVG from logo uploads (stored XSS vector).
- Frontend uses the signed url returned by the API.
- Tests: unit tests plus a MySQL integration test of upload, signed download, tenant isolation and
  deletion; enabled in CI via RUN_MYSQL_WARRANTY_TESTS.
