From: "Claude (audit & migration)" <claude@users.noreply.anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:43:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] security(proxy): trust proxies by CIDR and resolve the
 real client IP safely

- HttpsEnforcementMiddleware now uses the shared CIDR-aware matcher (IPv4/IPv6, IPv4-mapped), so
  platforms with non-fixed proxy addresses (Railway) no longer trigger redirect loops.
- RequestHelper: opt-in CLIENT_IP_HEADER (e.g. X-Real-IP) honoured only for trusted peers, and
  X-Forwarded-Client-IP authenticated by PROXY_SHARED_SECRET (hash_equals). No other headers trusted.
- Cloudflare Pages function: fail closed without BACKEND_URL, strip spoofable headers, forward the
  visitor IP only with the shared secret, and stop leaking network error details.
- Tests for CIDR trust, platform header, shared-secret flow and the proxy function.
