Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:43:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(deploy): Railway support (PORT-aware Apache,
 liveness healthcheck, env hydration)

- Dockerfile: Apache listens on $PORT via docker/entrypoint.sh (default 80); vhost/ports configs
  moved to docker/; PHP execution denied under public/uploads with nosniff + CSP; private storage dir;
  optional persistent volume (PERSIST_DIR) with logo symlink; HEALTHCHECK follows $PORT.
- railway.toml: Dockerfile builder, /check healthcheck, restart policy. render.yaml removed.
- /check is exempt from the HTTPS redirect (it returned 301 to plain-HTTP healthchecks).
- Environment::hydrateFromProcess(): platform variables reach $_ENV even when php.ini
  variables_order omits "E" (otherwise startup secret validation blocks the app).
- .env.production.example rewritten for Railway (reference variables, SMTP names, proxy settings).
- docs/RAILWAY_DEPLOYMENT.md, README and DEPLOYMENT_CHECKLIST updated for the Railway migration.
